+## RozeLynx Download Hand-off (General pane, USE=download-handoff)
+
+rozelynx-handoff-header = Download hand-off
+rozelynx-handoff-description =
+    Hand downloads off to a configured download manager before RozeLynx
+    builds any save UI. One list, in order: the first handler that accepts
+    a download gets it, and the rest are not tried.
+rozelynx-handoff-mode-label = Hand downloads off to
+    .title = “Whatever is available” hands off only when at least one enabled handler can take the download.
+rozelynx-handoff-mode-auto = whatever is available
+rozelynx-handoff-mode-always = always
+rozelynx-handoff-mode-never = never
+rozelynx-handoff-empty = No handlers. Downloads stay in the browser.
+rozelynx-handoff-new-id =
+    .placeholder = uget, ext:<extension> or cmd:<program>
+rozelynx-handoff-add-btn = Add
+rozelynx-handoff-hint =
+    “uget” is built in and speaks uget-integrator’s own protocol. “cmd:aria2c”
+    runs a program on your PATH with the args you give it, and
+    “ext:some@extension” asks another extension that answers download
+    messages. Args may use {url} {filename} {referer} {ua} and {cookies}.
